  "tagline": "Sasun's trance-inducing martial clap dance",
  "profile": "Yarkhushta (Յարխուշտա) is an Armenian folk and martial dance associated with the highlands of historic Sasun in Western Armenia, belonging to the category of Armenian \"clap dances\" (tsap parer). Men face one another in pairs, rapidly approach and vigorously clap the palms of the opposite dancer (Wikipedia). It is mentioned in the works of Movses Khorenatsi, Faustus of Byzantium and Grigor Magistros, indicating early-medieval origins, and was traditionally danced by soldiers before combat to cast off fear.",
  "insight": "The dance's loud zurna and deep bass-drum pairing produces a wide peak-to-peak sound amplitude that can place dancers in a euphoric, adrenaline-fueled trance; revived by the Maratuk and Karin ensembles, there have been efforts to introduce it into the Armenian Army's repertoire (Wikipedia).",
